#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""FS3 v210 - targeting, radar and target view (Silvio, 10.10.2026).

    Targeting  FreeSpace 2 keys (own settings tab TARGETING): T / Shift+T
               ships, H / Shift+H hostiles, F / Shift+F friendlies, Y the
               ship in the reticle, R the nearest ship attacking you,
               B / Shift+B bombs, S / Shift+S / V subsystems. A lost target
               (or none) becomes the nearest hostile at once (Silvio).
               Brackets in her side colour, the lead indicator of the
               primaries firing (only on the screen and within their reach,
               linked: the shorter one). Edge marker only for the target.
    Bar        Radar of the whole mission area with the MediaVP radar icons
               in the side colour, the target's model behind them in her
               real orientation (no flames), hull, shield and distance -
               one window between SUPPORT and the buttons. The columns
               beside it are a little narrower.
    Seekers    Aspect seekers need a lock on the target (FS2 $Min Lock
               Time, near the nose, within reach); without one they fly
               straight. Heat seekers take the target or the nearest heat
               source in their FS2 view cone. No seeker turns back over its
               own tail.
    Hits       Shots hit a capital ship where her model is drawn (sunk
               below the plane, seen in perspective): hullView/hullUnPt.
               Capital turrets fire from where they are drawn.
    Tempo      Back to the v208 pace and reach (TEMPO_K = 1). The hold
               ring, the pointer and the size of shots stay as in v209.
    Sky        Stars, planets and suns have no motion of their own in a
               wave; they move only with the camera, the nearer more.

Needs v209. Edits src/10_core.js, 20_render.js, 50_combat.js, 56_banks.js,
57_turrets.js, 59_field3d.js, 60_effects.js, 70_ui.js and the tests
wpnsim.js, fieldsim.js; new
src/71_radar_icons.js and src/72_target.js. No new model files.
Run assemble.py 210 afterwards.
"""
